Some overfitting patches don't crash — they return a wrong value. You cannot ask 'is this the right answer' (no reference is available), but you CAN assert a relation between two related calls of the target that must hold for ANY correct implementation. Add ONE such check after your normal calls: compute both sides from REAL library calls on the fuzzed input, and if they disagree, `throw new RuntimeException("metamorphic violation: <which relation>")`. Jazzer reports that as a finding, the same as a crash.

